# What may reach the build daemon. The Dockerfile copies explicit paths rather than
# `COPY . .`, so this file is not what decides the image contents — it decides what
# leaves this machine at all. Two jobs: keep credentials and local-only state out of a
# context that gets uploaded and cached, and stop a ~700 MB checkout being tarred up on
# every build of a service whose own source is a few dozen kilobytes.

# Secrets. .env holds INTAKE_IP_SALT and GITHUB_TOKEN on a development machine; both
# belong to the operator's env file on the VPS and to no image, ever. Excluded from the
# context rather than merely uncopied, so no future COPY can pick one up by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local-only workspace — invisible to git, and it must be invisible here for the same
# reason (private/README.md).
private/

# The intake queue from a local run. Operational state, never canonical: baking one in
# would ship somebody's pending submission and their hashed IP into a public image, and
# in sqlite mode the container would then start against a stale queue instead of the
# volume. Three files, because WAL mode.
intake.db
intake.db-*

# Reinstalled from the lockfile inside the image. Copying a host tree in would also
# import darwin/arm64 binaries into a linux/amd64 image.
node_modules/

# History and CI config. .git is the largest thing here after node_modules and the
# image needs none of it — server/batch.ts talks to the GitHub API, not to a checkout.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Expo/web build artefacts. dist/ in particular is the static export that Caddy serves
# from a host bind mount; it must not also exist inside the API image, where it could
# only ever be a stale second copy.
dist/
web/
web-build/
.expo/
expo-env.d.ts
public/markets.json
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo

# The app. Nothing here is imported by server/index.ts or server/batch.ts, and
# react-native must not sit anywhere behind a module a Node server loads. src/lib and
# src/constants are the only two subtrees the Dockerfile copies, and they stay in.
src/app/
src/components/
src/hooks/
src/types/
src/global.css
assets/
ios/
android/
.kotlin/

# Tooling, docs and prose. Read on GitHub, not in a container. `*.md` matches top-level
# files only — .dockerignore patterns do not cross a slash — so server/README.md rides
# along inside server/, which is where an operator in a shell would look for it.
.claude/
.vscode/
.playwright-mcp/
test/
docs/
*.md
LICENSE
REUSE.toml
eslint.config.js
app.json

# Compose and its example env: the deployment describes the image, the image does not
# contain the deployment.
compose.yaml
docker-compose.yml
Caddyfile
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.jks
*.mobileprovision
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
